WEBVTT

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.180
Universal Century 0096.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.380
Banagher Links,

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.720
a student attending
the Anaheim Electronics Industrial College

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.470
at the colony Industrial 7,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.930
has a fateful encounter with
a green-eyed girl falling from the sky.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.880
Prevent it? Prevent what?

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.090
War.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.930
As fighting begins within the colony,

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.930
Banagher returns to Magallanica to rescue
the girl who calls herself Audrey.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.220
His father Cardeas Vist entrusts him
with the Unicorn Gundam,

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.970
the key to Laplace's Box

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.550
which could
overturn the Federation government.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:39.970
Father...

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.380
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.680
I must...

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.930
...go!

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.590
The Unicorn Gundam is a key

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.130
designed to disclose the whereabouts
of Laplace's Box in stages.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:00.260
Caught between the Earth Federation Forces
and the Sleeves, led by Full Frontal,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.760
Banagher finds himself
dragged into a major conspiracy,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.680
the curse of the Universal Century.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.970
I never intended to kill, but...

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.720
I was about to be killed.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.970
I am not a murderer.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.130
The only way to activate the NT-D

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.180
is to get him to fight someone
who could be a Newtype.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.720
Ple Twelve.
That is her name.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.930
The 12th prototype.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.800
The coordinates shown by the Unicorn Gundam

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.590
are the ruins
of the prime minister's residence,

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.760
the space station Laplace,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.380
which was destroyed by a terrorist bombing
in the first year of the Universal Century.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.470
Banagher!

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.470
Something's coming.
The Nahel Argama is being targeted.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.680
Even a cog in the machine has its pride.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.930
You go fulfill your own role.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.180
My own...

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.550
This knows what it is.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.630
Banagher!

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.260
You killed him!

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.720
I'm gonna take you down
if nothing else!

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.300
At the same time,
Riddhe descends to Earth with Mineva,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.380
only to learn that his family
has deep ties to the Vist Foundation

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.760
through its relationship to Laplace's Box.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.380
And thus, he finds himself trapped by fate.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.880
I've brought you to the
worst possible place.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.090
And here I thought
I could help you...

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.590
Elsewhere, Banagher has been saved

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.970
by Captain Zinnerman
and the crew of the Garencieres,

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.180
who make a crash landing in the desert.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:20.300
(BATTLE AT TORRINGTON)

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.090
We were prisoners of war
here in Africa.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:57.010
In the camp, the Treaty didn't
count for anything, but that's okay.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.800
Zeons are Zeons.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.180
To the Feds, we were the devils
who'd dropped a colony.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.470
While the bigwigs were
negotiating a peace,

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:11.630
the Fed troops sent to occupy our
homeland were getting frustrated.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.880
They'd been brought up on stuff like,

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.010
"Kill the demonic Zeon!" and "If you
want a woman, get one in Zeon!"

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.840
They needed a scapegoat
to appease them.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:29.470
And then one night, a town was overrun
by soldiers who came out of nowhere.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.930
The elderly, begging for their lives,
children clinging to their mothers,

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.970
they killed every last person.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.800
Officially, it was written off as
troops pacifying rioting citizens,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.840
but it was obvious to everyone
that they were blowing off steam.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.970
That town's name was Globe.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.880
My mom and dad lived there.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.680
So did the Captain's family.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:57.590
His wife and their daughter,
who'd just turned five...

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.630
The revival of Zeon wouldn't
bring any of them back,

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.800
and I don't give a rat's ass
what's inside that box.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:22.130
But do we die in vain,
cursing the world?

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.800
Or do we keep fighting
an endless war?

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.760
Those were our two choices.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.880
Why are you crying?

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.090
It's so beautiful.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:42.630
It almost makes you doubt all those
stories about the Earth being polluted.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:46.380
Thing is, the air around here is even
more polluted than it used to be.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.630
And they say the desert has advanced
all the way to Dakar's doorstep.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.130
It's all humanity's doing.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.880
Indiscriminate development, the
dropped colonies and asteroid...

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.380
If humanity is the
product of nature,

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.880
that makes all of mankind's trash
and poison natural products, too.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.680
And even if it's rendered unfit
for human habitation,

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:12.470
I guess that'll be the result of
nature achieving a new balance.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:15.300
Mother nature has
absolutely no mercy.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:18.260
Ancient humans understood that.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:22.050
As products of nature,
they knew it instinctively.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:27.880
So to survive, they protected themselves
by creating civilization and societies.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:32.050
Yeah. But they got too complicated,
and before they knew it,

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:36.970
people were forced to live for the
purpose of maintaining the system.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:40.840
In the end, it made life
hard to live.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.970
And to escape that topsy-turvy world,
they went into space to find new lands.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.470
There, they created
a different system.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:53.470
A natural development that
gave hope and direction

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.260
to those cast out into space,
the Spacenoids.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.430
That was Zeon.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:02.380
The old system left behind
on Earth rejected it.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.970
Because systems from two different
birthplaces are never compatible.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.840
It always ends with one of them trying
to force the other into submission.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.930
But in the past, a world with a unified
government like the Federation

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.760
and ten billion people
living in space

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.590
must have sounded
like a fairy tale.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.930
Doesn't humanity have
the possibility to do it?

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:26.220
To make two ways of thinking
merge into one someday?

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.470
We all aren't governed
fairly and equally.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:35.430
The hatred of the beaten and downtrodden
clings to the Earth to this day.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.220
That's a sad thing.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:43.260
Yeah... I suppose it is.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:47.760
Even though we live our lives
trying to escape sadness...

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.970
I wonder why that is?

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:02.550
Banagher.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:07.050
I know, I know. A man doesn't cry
in front of other people, right?

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.340
No.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.050
Crying because you care
is a different matter.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:18.970
I don't trust people who
never cry, no matter what.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.050
Banagher.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.180
I owe you.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:53.720
If it weren't for you, I might've
given up along the way, too.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.220
Don't thank me, all I did
was slow you down.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:01.260
Having someone to butt heads
with can make all the difference.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.630
Does the Garencieres Team
have a new member?

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.050
That's a bad habit, Captain.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.010
Okay, stop right there!

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.300
Good work.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.380
Captain.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.430
Someone once told me to think of
a better way to use the Box.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.630
What if that's my...

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:30.340
Where is it? Where is the Unicorn's
next set of coordinates?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.090
It's Torrington this time, eh?

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:36.470
This Box certainly keeps giving us
one difficult location after the other.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:41.590
It makes me wonder if we're being
played for fools by Cardeas Vist.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:45.680
Nicely done at Dakar,
Lt. Commander Kirks.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:49.970
Thanks to your distracting them
with your Earth Zeon Remnants,

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.180
we were able to protect
the Garencieres.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.510
You have my gratitude.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.590
And you ours, sir.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:59.090
The Zee Zulus
proved to be formidable assets.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.220
Ah, you must be Ensign Loni Garvey.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.130
I am familiar with your father.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.340
He has done us a great service,
perfecting Haman's legacy as he did.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.930
Captain, my life's sole purpose is
to settle the scores that haunt the souls

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.840
of my father and mother,
and their comrades.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:15.800
Loni!

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.800
I would like you to assign us
the mission to attack Torrington.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.930
If we unload the
Split-horn Gundam there,

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:25.630
we should learn the whereabouts
of Laplace's Box.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.300
I lead the Neo Zeon who have made
their stronghold in space.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:35.340
I have no right to issue orders
to you and your forces,

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.470
who have been waging a guerilla war
on Earth since the One Year War.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.430
In that case, may I take that to mean
that you also have no right to stop us?

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.970
May the heavens protect the heir
to Mahdi's cause.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.260
Sieg Zeon!

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:01.380
Captain, is this wise?

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.840
Dakar was bad enough, but this will- -

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.340
I understand
your misgivings, Captain.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:09.340
Nevertheless, they have been
waiting all this time.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.930
Waiting while time
stood still around them.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.590
People grow accustomed
to waiting.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.630
I expect that they could have
gone on waiting forever.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:23.300
However, time has begun to flow again.
Because of Cardeas Vist's actions.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:27.720
If we do nothing, the waters will
only become hopelessly muddied.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.430
Do you not agree, Captain?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:35.680
To prevent that, I have another job
for the Garencieres.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.010
- Here you go.
- Sure thing.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.680
So, you're the pilot
of the Split-horn.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:45.630
The key to the Box.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:46.590
Key?

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.010
I expect great things from you.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.800
They say she was piloting
the behemoth at Dakar.

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.680
A girl like her?

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.590
Message from Kirks Team!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.180
The ones who
attacked Dakar, huh?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.380
This is a code used by
the old Principality.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.510
It's a watchword dating back to
the Third Landing Operation,

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.380
when our first forces came down
to Earth during the One Year War.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:22.720
What does it say?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:27.840
"About to give the Feds the shock
of their lives! Request assistance!

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:30.010
Dakar was only the beginning!"

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.720
Dolphin 02, signal lost!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.180
Damage report!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.380
Sonar, waiting for explosion sounds
to die down.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.010
Aquatic ordnance, all green.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.680
Propulsion, values nominal!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.680
Dolphin 01, still engaging
two unknown mobile suits!

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.970
Can we launch
our reserve suits?!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:44.760
Three minutes until flooding
is complete!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.800
They say we're to drop
this off at the coordinate point

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:12.710
once the base is captured,
then wait for new info to be revealed.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.380
They say Ivan's
gonna be our escort.

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.460
What's wrong, Banagher?

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:23.710
It's strange. You know, for Zeon weapons
to fit a Federation mobile suit.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:28.510
That's 'cause both sides
use a universal standard.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:32.800
If their parts can get along,
why can't they quit fighting?

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:37.090
That's the one thing that mellowed out
while they were fighting.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.380
It was more efficient that way.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.170
You mean it worked better
for Anaheim Electronics?

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:46.590
And it worked better in the field, too.
It's helping us right now, right?

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.090
That's it, huh?

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:08.460
He's good.

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.510
We are on a course
for New Guinea.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:17.590
The Federation Forces submarine Bonefish
has gone missing in the Coral Sea.

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:21.630
Given the state of the scene, there is
a strong possibility that she was sunk.

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:24.380
If this is related to the camouflaged
ship we are hunting,

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.210
we may encounter and engage
the enemy with no warning.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:32.590
Our top priority is to secure Laplace's
Box, but we may not have that luxury.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.340
Stay sharp while you
are out there.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:35.630
Yes, sir!

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.260
- Captain Bright.
- What is it?

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:44.760
I'd appreciate it if you would stop
giving me special treatment.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:49.210
Whatever my background,
I am an E.F.S.F. pilot.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.300
Please don't take me off
dangerous missions to- -

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.420
Get over yourself!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:58.590
Thinking that way proves that you are
giving yourself special treatment.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:02.840
I never had any intention of doing so,
no matter who you are.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:05.090
If I need you, I will use you.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:08.670
However, if you launch, make sure
that you come back alive.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:12.670
If you can do that, I'll see you
as a pilot like any other.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:13.960
Yes, sir.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:18.130
It's me.
Put it through.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.460
It's Bright.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.130
What did you say?!

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:31.710
Why do you suppose
it's that place?

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.210
It's where the colony
was dropped.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.300
Damn that Cardeas Vist...

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:40.920
Is he trying to make us retrace the path
of humanity's downfall or something?

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.340
That kid will be fine.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:46.260
Still, if he defied us for real
in that suit,

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.760
we couldn't do a thing to stop him.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:51.340
Right now, he has
total faith in you, Captain.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.340
Ms. Loni...

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.130
Massive mobile armor
approaching from shore!

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:24.550
Torrington Base, requesting assistance!

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:01.010
Russet, Candor! Scatter!
The next wave is coming!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.380
Loni! Avoid the city!

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:05.380
There's no need to take a detour.

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:07.670
Have you forgotten what
the Federation did to us?

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:10.420
It'll create unnecessary casualties.
Keep your cool!

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:11.460
Acknowledged...

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:13.510
What?!

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:14.920
What's the matter, Loni?

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:16.760
Father?

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:46.340
A Psycommu runaway...
Is it thirsty for blood or something?!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:51.840
This is a... This is nothing
but a slaughter!

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:57.510
This doesn't seem like an act of people
who see themselves as Char's successors.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:58.460
How many?

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:03.340
There are four small transports and
one mid-sized VTOL craft above the area.

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:08.510
Do you think I'm lucky enough for that
to be the camouflaged freighter?

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.920
I've intercepted the enemy's
trunk line, sir!

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.050
This is the group
that attacked Dakar?

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:17.260
All hands, level two battle stations!
Mobile suits on standby!

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:21.590
Are these people connected
to the Box, too?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.380
Audrey, I suppose you and I
can't escape the curse

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.130
of the families we were born into.

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:36.050
Is this just more useless struggling?

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.300
Hey, newbie!

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:40.210
If you ever slow us down,
I'll shoot you in the back if I have to.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.760
Remember that.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.340
This seems like a fine team.
I wish I could have joined.

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:48.550
You can join whenever you want.
Just shoot one of us three in the back.

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:49.840
I'll keep that in mind.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:51.960
Pilots have to fight
believing in their orders,

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:53.630
even if their bosses are morons.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:58.170
We lucked out there. At least
we serve under a great C.O.

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:01.840
The commander of the Gundam Corps...

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:05.210
Gundam...
The key to the Box.

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:41.550
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:43.460
A PRIVATE WAR

